    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0451" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2536</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the British Chargé</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Barclay</hi>)</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>The Secretary of State has the honor to acknowledge the receipt of the memorandum
                    of His Majesty’s Chargé d’Affaires, of August 16, 1918,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d437-f1"/> informing him of the instructions sent by the British
                    Government to the British Consul at Vladivostok in connection with the methods
                    deemed essential by the British Government in order to establish order in that
                    city; and further requesting that, if this Government concur, similar
                    instructions be sent to the American representatives at Vladivostok.</p>
                <p>The Department of State has been happy to take under consideration the
                    suggestions advanced by His Britannic Majesty’s Chargé d’Affaires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-31"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 31, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
